{
    "background_story": "Boden was a free-spirited artist who lived life on his own terms. He spent his days painting vibrant murals on city walls and his nights playing guitar in local bars. His carefree nature drew people to him, and he had a large circle of friends who admired his creativity. But one day, without warning, Boden was gone. He left behind only a cryptic note and a half-finished canvas in his studio. Some said he had grown tired of the city and sought inspiration in the wilderness, while others whispered that he had been struggling with inner demons. Despite the mystery surrounding his departure, Boden's art remained, a testament to the impact he had on those who knew him. His friends continued to create, inspired by the memories of the charismatic artist who had vanished into thin air.",
